''a''-<sup>3</sup>, ''a''-<sup>4</sup>.] A reduced form of ''of'', now generally written ''o''’, as in man-''o''’-war, six ''o''’clock, etc.
{{smaller block|The name of John ''a'' Gaunt.{{right|''Shak.'', Rich. II., i. 3.}}
It’s sixe ''a'' clocke.{{right|''B. Jonson'', Every Man in his Humor, i. 4.}}}}

'''a'''<sup>5</sup> (a), ''pron.'' [E. dial., corruption of ''I'', being the first element, obscured, of the diphthong äi.] A modern provincial corruption of the pronoun ''I''.

'''a'''<sup>6</sup> (ạ), ''pron.'' [E. dial., < ME. dial. ''a'', corruptly for ''he'', he, ''heo'', she, ''he'', it, ''heo'', ''hi'', they.] An old (and modern provincial) corruption of all genders and both numbers of the third personal pronoun, he, she, it, they. So ''quotha'', that is, ''quoth he''.
{{smaller block|''A'' babbled of green fields.{{right|''Shak.'', Hen. V., ii. 3.}}}}

'''a'''<sup>7</sup> (ạ), ''v.'' [E. dial., < ME. ''a'', ''ha'', reduced form of ''have'', the ''v'' being dropped as in ''a''<sup>4</sup> or ''o''’ for ''of'' (ov).] An old (and modern provincial) corruption of ''have'' as an auxiliary verb, unaccented, and formerly also as a principal verb.
{{smaller block|I had not thought my body could ''a'' yielded.{{right|''Beau. and Fl.''}}}}

'''a'''<sup>8</sup> (â). [Sc., usually written ''a''’, = E. ''all'', like Sc. ''ca''’ = E. ''call'', ''fa''’ = ''fall'', ''ha''’ = ''hall'', etc.] All.
{{smaller block|<poem>For ''a''’ that, an’ ''a''’ that,
His riband, star, an’ ''a''’ that,
The man o’ independent mind,
He looks an’ laughs at ''a''’ that.</poem>
{{right|''Burns'', For A’ That.}}}}
